{"v":2,"s":"m","w":8,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Solving linear equations","b":"<p>A linear equation has x only to the first power. Steps:</p><ol><li>Remove brackets.</li><li>If there are fractions, multiply everything by the NZS of the denominators.</li><li>Move x terms to one side and numbers to the other (change the sign when you move).</li><li>Divide by the coefficient of x.</li><li>Check by substituting.</li></ol><div class=\"callout\">A balance scale: whatever you do to one side, do to the other and it stays level.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 154\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"An equation is a balance: do the same thing to both sides and it stays level.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M160 120 L146 146 H174 Z\" class=\"ink\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"108\" class=\"k\" /><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"120\" class=\"k\" /><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"72\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"72\" class=\"km\" /><rect x=\"40\" y=\"58\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"a2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">3x + 2</text><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"72\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"72\" class=\"km\" /><rect x=\"200\" y=\"58\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" class=\"a2\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">11</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"12\">−2 on both sides → 3x = 9 → x = 3</text></svg><figcaption>An equation is a balance: do the same thing to both sides and it stays level.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Special cases","b":"<ul><li>0 · x = 5 → <b>no solution</b>.</li><li>0 · x = 0 → <b>every number</b> is a solution.</li></ul>"},{"t":"read","h":"Linear inequalities","b":"<p>Solve them the same way, with one rule: <b>multiplying or dividing by a negative number flips the sign</b>.</p><div class=\"fx\">−2x > 6  ⇒  x < −3</div><p>Write the answer as an interval: x < −3 is (−∞, −3).</p>"},{"t":"ex","q":"(x − 1)/2 − (x + 1)/3 = 1","s":["Multiply by 6: 3(x − 1) − 2(x + 1) = 6.","Expand: 3x − 3 − 2x − 2 = 6.","Simplify: x − 5 = 6 → x = 11.","Check: 10/2 − 12/3 = 5 − 4 = 1 ✓"],"a":"x = 11"},{"t":"num","q":"5x − 3 = 2x + 9. x = ?","a":4,"u":"","e":"3x = 12."},{"t":"num","q":"2(x − 3) = x + 1. x = ?","a":7,"u":"","e":"2x − 6 = x + 1."},{"t":"num","q":"x/4 + 1 = 3. x = ?","a":8,"u":"","e":"x/4 = 2."},{"t":"mc","q":"Solve −2x > 6:","o":["x > −3","x < −3","x > 3","x < 3"],"a":1,"e":"Dividing by −2 flips the sign."},{"t":"tf","q":"The equation 0 · x = 7 has no solution.","a":true,"e":"No number times 0 gives 7."}]}